[31m-// =============================================================================[m
[31m-// mapping_controller.sv[m
[31m-// =============================================================================[m
[31m-// Description:[m
[31m-//   Reads a 24-row x 256-col pixel matrix from memory (72-bit words,[m
[31m-//   4 pixels/word, 18 bits/pixel) and produces 5x5 sliding-window outputs[m
[31m-//   over a 24x24 pixel buffer.[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-//   *** 4-WINDOW-PARALLEL EDIT ***[m
[31m-//   Instead of outputting one 5x5 window per cycle (400 cycles per interior[m
[31m-//   24x24 region), this version outputs WIN_GROUP=4 consecutive horizontal[m
[31m-//   windows per cycle, reducing FETCH time by 4x (100 cycles interior).[m
[31m-//   The output bus is widened from 450 bits (25x18) to 1800 bits (100x18).[m
[31m-//   All LOAD, bank-rotation, and padding logic is UNCHANGED.[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-// MEMORY LAYOUT[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-//   Full matrix : 24 rows x 256 cols[m
[31m-//   Word width  : 72 bits = 4 pixels x 18 bits[m
[31m-//   Row r base  : r * 64  (64 words per row)[m
[31m-//   1-cycle read latency: address presented cycle N, data valid cycle N+1[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-// BUFFER ORGANISATION  (banks store COLUMNS, not rows)[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-//   The 24x24 pixel buffer is split into 3 column-banks:[m
[31m-//     bank 0 : 24 rows x cols  0.. 7[m
[31m-//     bank 1 : 24 rows x cols  8..15[m
[31m-//     bank 2 : 24 rows x cols 16..23[m
[31m-//   buf[bank][row][col_within_bank]  col_within_bank = 0..7[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-// HORIZONTAL SLIDING  (30 windows across 256 cols)[m
[31m-// --------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[31m-//   Window k covers pixel-cols 8k .. 8k+23  (k = 0..29)[m
[31m-//   In memory, pixel-col C is at word offset C/4 within its row.[m
[31m-//   Window k reads word offsets 2k .. 2k+5  (6 words = 24 pixels per row).[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-//   Full load  (first window or new sweep):[m
[31m-//     Read 6 words x 24 rows = 144 words.[m
[31m-//     Words 0..1 per row  -> bank 0 (cols 0..7)[m
[31m-//     Words 2..3 per row  -> bank 1 (cols 8..15)[m
[31m-//     Words 4..5 per row  -> bank 2 (cols 16..23)[m
[31m-//[m
[31m-//   Partial load (windows 1..29 within a sweep):[m
[31m-//     Only the rightmost 8 new pixel-columns enter the window.[m
[31m-//     Read 2 words x 24 rows = 48 words  (word offsets 2k+4, 2k+5 per row).[m
[31m-//     These 48 words overwrite write_bank  (the bank that held the oldest cols).[m
[31m-//[m
